Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||01-20-2001||10:27 PM||||Some questions:<P>1. In the 1985-1987 model years were any Fieros built with the Iron Duke mated to a 5 speed Getrag. <P>2. If there were any of the above would a 2.8 V-6 mate up to the manual tranny in these cars.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||01-20-2001||10:32 PM||||4 cyl 5 sp were all  Isuzu trannys,  only the V6 had Getrags but both trannys have the same bolt pattern so all combos will bolt toghther. Confusing huh?<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||01-20-2001||11:00 PM||||Here's the deal:<P>Almost any GM transverse engine will bolt to almost any transverse transaxle.<BR>Almost any GM longitudinal engine will bolt to almsot any longitudinal transmission.<BR>To mix and match the two requires an adapter plate.<P>The only GM 4 cylinder to have a Getrag was the Quad 4. That transaxle is quad 4 specific because of the starter location.<BR>All iron ducks use the Isuzu transmission.||||reg||1
